,"number":14,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 15","number":15,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 16","number":16,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 17","number":17,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 18","number":18,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 19","number":19,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 20","number":20,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]}],"assets":[],"contentBlocks":[{"sequence":0,"text":"## Problem Statement\n\nYesterday was a fair in a supermarket's grocery section. There were n jars with spices on the fair. Before the event the jars were numbered from 1 to n from the left to the right. After the event the jars were moved and the grocer had to sort them by the increasing of the numbers.\n\nThe grocer has a special machine at his disposal. The machine can take any 5 or less jars and rearrange them in the way the grocer wants. Note that the jars do not have to stand consecutively. For example, from the permutation 2 , 6 , 5 , 4 , 3 , 1 one can get permutation 1 , 2 , 3 , 4 , 5 , 6 , if pick the jars on the positions 1 , 2 , 3 , 5 and 6 . \n\nWhich minimum number of such operations is needed to arrange all the jars in the order of their numbers' increasing?\n\n## Input\n\nThe first line contains an integer n ( 1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë n ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 5 ). The second line contains n space-separated integers a i ( 1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë a i ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë n ) ΓÇö the i -th number represents the number of a jar that occupies the i -th position. It is guaranteed that all the numbers are distinct.\n\n## Output\n\nPrint on the first line the least number of operations needed to rearrange all the jars in the order of the numbers' increasing. Then print the description of all actions in the following format.\n\nOn the first line of the description of one action indicate the number of jars that need to be taken ( k ), on the second line indicate from which positions the jars need to be taken ( b 1 ,ΓÇë b 2 ,ΓÇë...,ΓÇë b k ), on the third line indicate the jar's new order ( c 1 ,ΓÇë c 2 ,ΓÇë...,ΓÇë c k ). After the operation is fulfilled the jar from position b i will occupy the position c i . The set ( c 1 ,ΓÇë c 2 ,ΓÇë...,ΓÇë c k ) should be the rearrangement of the set ( b 1 ,ΓÇë b 2 ,ΓÇë...,ΓÇë b k ).\n\nIf there are multiple solutions, output any.\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n6\n3 5 6 1 2 4\n```\n```\n2\n4\n1 3 6 4 \n3 6 4 1 \n2\n2 5 \n5 2\n```\n\n## Note\n\nLet's consider the first sample. The jars can be sorted within two actions.\n\nDuring the first action we take the jars from positions 1 , 3 , 6 and 4 and put them so that the jar that used to occupy the position 1 will occupy the position 3 after the operation is completed. The jar from position 3 will end up in position 6 , the jar from position 6 will end up in position 4 and the jar from position 4 will end up in position 1 .\n\nAfter the first action the order will look like that: 1 , 5 , 3 , 4 , 2 , 6 . \n\nDuring the second operation the jars in positions 2 and 5 will change places.","type":"text"}],"contestId":91,"index":"D","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Grocer's Problem","problemKey":"91-D","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"2 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/91/problem/D"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","